family: line-cli
what: syslog
transport: udp
address: 192.0.2.20
verification: reference
reference: common line-oriented logging commands (logging host, logging trap, logging facility, logging source-interface); RFC 5424 severities
does: Sends the device's log messages, informational and more severe, to Woodshed over UDP.
check: The device appears on Woodshed's Dashboard with its first message; if it doesn't, check the device's log host status and Woodshed's Listeners on the Setup page.
placeholders: 
addresses: 192.0.2.20 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- `logging host 192.0.2.20` alone sends over UDP to port 514 on most devices of this style.
- `logging trap` sets the lowest severity sent to log hosts on many devices; others set it on the host line, or accept the number (6) instead of the keyword.
- Turn on timestamps in the messages if the device offers it (with milliseconds and the time zone, where it can); Woodshed also keeps the time each message arrived.
---- part cli "": Enter in global configuration mode, fill in the placeholders, then save the configuration
logging host 192.0.2.20
logging trap informational
